This directory contains the SLATEC library from NETLIB [1]. The directory
'src' contains the source files and the directory 'old' contains the original
versions of the source file 'd1mach.f', 'i1mach.f', and 'r1mach.f'. The
versions in the source directory 'src' of these files are modified versions of
these source files.

The source files 'd1mach.f' and 'r1mach.f' use Fortran 95 intrinsic functions
to obtain the machine constants. The expressions for the machine constants in
terms of these intrinsic functions have been obtained from John Burkhardt's
webpage [2]. (Note however that there is an ambiguity on that webpage: 'log'
denotes the base 10 logarithm and not the natural logarithm.) The use of
these intrinsic functions make these source files portable, however, you need
a Fortran 95 compiler to compile these files.

The source file 'i1mach.f' in 'src' is the version provided by 'slatec4linux'
on the webpage [1]. I (Halil Cakir) am not sure how to make all of the
definitions of that file portable.

[1] http://www.netlib.org/slatec/ (retrieved: 2017/07/27)
[2] http://people.sc.fsu.edu/~jburkardt/f_src/machine/machine.html
    (retrieved: 2017/07/27)

